WEBVTT

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.630
And the second players' match 
has come to a grand close!

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.520
Rinkai Girls' still continues to lead!

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.510
But Usuzan High School and Yamasu High School

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.880
were putting up a great fight, too!

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.050
This is the moment you've all waited for!

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.740
The third players' match will be...

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.500
...right after lunch!

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.600
<i>Good work.</i>

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.020
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.320
What are you doing for lunch, Sukoyan?

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:05.540
<b>Hand 6: 
Withering</b>

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.660
I thought I'd eat one of the 
bentos they've got here.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.650
Then I'll have a bento, too!

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.810
Kokaji-san...

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.780
<i>And...</i>

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.030
<i>some strange woman.</i>

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.800
Yasuko-chan...

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.880
You were doing analysis for the 
Rinkai Girls' match today, right?

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.250
You've been working hard.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.750
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.430
That reminds me.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.690
Did you see yesterday's game?

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:36.800
The one with Akado...

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:38.680
Yes...

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.040
Actually, we were doing the live 
commentary for another block,

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.010
so I didn't see it firsthand...

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:44.430
Huh?

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.330
What are you talking about?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.530
Oh, well, a long time ago,

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:52.020
there was someone I competed with

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.350
in the inter-high called Akado-san.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.780
I'm pretty sure she was playing 
on a pro team until recently,

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.360
but now she's leading

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.170
her old school's team to this 
tournament as their coach.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.320
I see.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:09.160
Well, I was just going to mention that 
her school's doing surprisingly well.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.630
Amazing, isn't it?

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:11.710
<i>That's it?</i>

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:16.060
So are you here as an analyst today?

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.980
No, actually I'm here for—

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.280
Hey, you're all here.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.220
What's this? What're you all talking about?

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.050
On a different topic,

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:34.190
isn't she another coach who 
has "aka" in her name?

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.110
She is a bit of a pain...

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.250
See you later.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.700
Good work.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:42.360
Thank you.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.380
Why are they going back the way they came?

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.620
Huh?

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:52.130
This bento is actually pretty tasty.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.880
So about the upcoming third players' match...

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:58.890
I was wondering if I should 
bring up the connection

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.260
between Eisui's third player and you.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.640
I wonder who's catering this event?

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.270
Want to go to the actual 
restaurant next time?

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.590
The restaurant that makes the bentos.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.350
Dinner will be a bit more expensive,

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:19.400
but it will obviously also be 
that much more delicious.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:23.780
What's wrong?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.620
Good.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.770
A normal reply would suffice.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.540
I am really sorry.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.660
That opponent was beyond our expectations.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.290
Toyone and I will take care of this.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.850
Don't worry, A-chan.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.380
What about me?

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:43.590
Aislinn-san has helped us out a lot in the past.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.350
Just one loss or a hundred is no problem at all.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.260
If anything, our score's still too high!

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.510
It's tiring when people cry on me.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.300
Try not to cry so much.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:02.790
There.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.580
By the way, are you all okay with 
not seeing the second matches?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.130
No, I actually really, really 
want to see them, but...

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.530
If we don't build up our strength,

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:22.250
we won't be able to battle the 
very opponents we want to watch.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.230
That's true...

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:29.350
but there might be others here 
who'd like to watch the matches.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.930
Oh, don't worry about me. I don't mind.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.400
Well, all right then.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.640
But there's a TV in the lobby,

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.800
so you can watch it there anytime.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.140
Oh, that's right.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:47.810
Risen-san is from Kagoshima, so 
you've played against Jindai Komaki.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:48.570
That's right.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.450
We may have come in second to Eisui Girls'

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.950
in the team tournament, 
but I personally do not

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.400
feel like I lost to her.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.500
I aim to prove this fact in 
the individual tournament.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:06.760
That's why I don't see this as 
letting you all practice on me.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.000
When Kei-san told me about this,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.920
I came because I thought it might 
be a chance to improve a bit myself.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.160
I see.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.520
No need to hold back, then. 
Let's all do our best!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.860
Let's do our best.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.110
Yeah!

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.930
Aww, man!

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:23.930
Jeez, Shizu.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.190
Sorry.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:31.090
<i>That said, I don't want Jindai 
Komaki to lose to anyone but myself.</i>

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:36.310
Should we just eat after the game?

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:37.790
I think so.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.290
Let's do that.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.130
Banana.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:42.630
Check.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.130
Toilet.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.440
Check.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.050
<b>Banana and Milk 
Eyewash 
Toilet 
Cold Compress</b>

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.430
All right.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.870
Guess it's time.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.400
You're leaving already?

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:54.250
There's still 15 minutes left of lunch.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.060
Yeah, but...

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.460
I'm itching to play so much, I can't stay still.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:00.310
I'm off.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:09.320
She seemed kind of strange.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.260
<i>Wow, this is huge.</i>

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:35.080
<i>This is quite different from 
where we played the first round.</i>

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:42.130
<i>I'll be going up against two of the</i>

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:44.480
<i>top eight schools in the nation right here.</i>

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.330
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.170
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:13.360
<i>How many minutes have I been standing here?</i>

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:25.270
<i>Thanks to Yuuki and Mako, 
we have this many points.</i>

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.200
<i>I've got to take good care of them.</i>

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.640
<i>I bet everyone from the prefectural 
preliminaries is watching, too.</i>

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.380
<i>I've got to win this.</i>

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:41.790
<i>I wonder why I feel kind of... 
lonely, sitting here right now.</i>

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:43.480
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.350
The captain sat down!

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.720
It took her a while

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.510
from the time she left the waiting room.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.510
Oh, the game is starting.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.260
The third players' match has begun!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.850
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 Third Player - 1st Year
 Takimi Haru

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.810
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
 Third Player - 3rd Year
 Kakura Kurumi

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.770
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 Third Player - 3rd Year
 Atago Hiroe

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.940
Fourth Turn

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.940
East Hand 1

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.940
Dealer - Takimi Haru

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:12.230
Hey. Yo, Kiyosumi!

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.310
I can see it.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.240
Your 3 of characters.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:22.740
<i>Oh, man... I haven't exposed a tile 
like that since grade school!</i>

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:28.500
<i>This is the top scoring player from 
Kiyosumi who defeated Ryuumonbuchi?</i>

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:30.610
<i>Is she nervous?</i>

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.100
<i>I can't tell if she's a novice or an idiot.</i>

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:35.350
<i>That's kind of disappointing.</i>

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:35.720
<i>Huh?</i>

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.350
Well then, why don't I liven things up?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.510
Have a riichi to start us off!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.230
First come, first serve.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.230
<i>She's crazy!</i>

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.000
<i>A riichi on the fifth turn.</i>

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.790
<i>I'm still three tiles from tenpai.</i>

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:58.070
<i>For safe tiles, I've only got 
the one she just played.</i>

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:06.660
It's comin'! My ippatsu is comin'!

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.670
What?! Why a 6 of circles?!

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.780
<i>The 6 of circles...</i>

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:15.130
<i>Then I'll go with this.</i>

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:16.880
That would be ron.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:19.880
5,200.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.510
<i>Ouch?</i>

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.220
My suji trap following the riichi is working.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.730
Don't forget that they call me 
"Hiroe the After-Riichi Suji Trapper."

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.400
I'm not dealer anymore...

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.600
I'm rolling the dice.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.860
But I mean, it's a coincidence that...

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.780
You talk too much.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:46.500
<i>I can't concentrate.</i>

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.380
<i>Oh, jeez...</i>

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.380
South Hand 3

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.380
Third Players' Match,
1st Half

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.160
<i>It's South Hand 3 and I 
haven't won a single time yet.</i>

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:59.310
<i>I guess this happens when 
you've played as often as I have.</i>

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:01.260
<i>It's not just that, though.</i>

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:07.800
<i>I don't think I can blame 
this on bad luck alone today.</i>

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:15.030
<i>I'm at Nationals. Maybe they 
are simply just that good.</i>

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.020
<i>Lookin' good!</i>

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.990
<i>I was worried about Kiyosumi, 
but she's not doing a thing.</i>

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.990
<i>Or maybe she can't do anything?</i>

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.370
<i>She's nothing but a dimwitted fool!</i>

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.580
<i>I didn't think having a dimwit at the table</i>

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.540
<i>would make things so much easier for me.</i>

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.670
<i>I gotta be grateful.</i>

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.090
<i>There's that, but...</i>

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:42.470
Ron.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.930
18,000.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.780
What's that look for?

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:49.810
Didn't you even have an 
inkling that I was in tenpai?

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.730
Kinda gets boring when 
you're too dimwitted.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.130
The current leader, Himematsu,

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.200
scores an 18,000 point direct 
hit on last place Kiyosumi.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.050
We're in South Hand 3 of 
the third players' match,

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:14.580
and dealer Atago Hiroe just 
increased her lead with a haneman.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.750
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.340
<i>Opponents at the Nationals will be tough,</i>

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.530
<i>even for Nodoka and Saki.</i>

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.930
<i>That's why I wanted to pad our 
lead in this third players' match.</i>

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.560
<i>And what's happening with that?</i>

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.640
<i>Instead of providing them with a 
buffer, I put us into last place!</i>

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.650
<i>At this rate... we could even be eliminated!</i>

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.840
<i>This year's my last year at the inter-high.</i>

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.540
<i>Even if we reach the finals, 
that's only six more East-South matches.</i>

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:45.530
<i>No, only five more that I'll get to play.</i>

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.260
<i>If I lose here, everything will</i>

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.290
<i>be over after the next East-South match.</i>

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.360
<i>Just one more East-South match?!</i>

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.160
<i>You've gotta be kidding me!</i>

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.300
<i>That's way too boring!</i>

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:08.390
<i>Didn't someone else say "boring" just now?</i>

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.730
Kinda gets boring when 
you're too dimwitted.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.560
<i>She's trying to have fun.</i>

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:17.990
<i>That's it.</i>

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.800
<i>I may have misunderstood.</i>

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:25.560
<i>The people from Nagano, 
the people cheering us on,</i>

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:28.990
<i>and my teammates are really important.</i>

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.120
<i>But it's not about them.</i>

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:34.630
<i>Right here and now,</i>

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:37.460
<i>if I, myself, am not having fun...</i>

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.410
<i>Nothing will ever start!</i>

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.720
<i>Looks like the dimwit got some life in her.</i>

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.270
Now we can finally play some 
inter-high level mahjong.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.230
Dealer, hurry up and draw.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.190
South Hand 3
Bonus 1

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.760
<i>This is a good draw.</i>

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:05.290
<i>Nodoka would probably 
laugh if I told her that</i>

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.240
<i>changing my mood changed my game.</i>

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:18.950
<i>Right after the dealer discarded 
the first East tile, this...</i>

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.720
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.170
<i>Tenpai.</i>

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.780
<i>Come on. You know that's not the one.</i>

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.180
Riichi!

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.100
<i>There it is.</i>

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:53.910
<i>Kiyosumi's bad wait.</i>

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.540
<b>Kiyosumi</b>

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:57.540
What?

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:02.280
I can't believe she threw away pinfu 
and iipeikou and the red dora!

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:03.290
That's crazy!

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.550
I am relieved, though.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.800
The captain didn't seem like 
herself before, so I was nervous.

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:11.970
You're right!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.590
I guess you're right...

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.740
Until now, I felt relieved because

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:20.100
she wasn't using many of those 
nervewracking plays of hers.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.360
Wait, the things that make us 
nervous are totally opposite!

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.780
Wow, when did you learn that 
kind of delayed comeback?

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.380
<i>She went sort of crazy by herself,</i>

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:32.240
<i>and then she got herself 
back to normal by herself.</i>

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.620
<i>Is she really going to be okay?</i>

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.950
<i>East... Huh?</i>

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:53.840
Tsumo!

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.390
That's 4,100 and 8,100.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:02.890
I think I'm getting into my game now.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.370
<i>Not bad.</i>

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:10.900
<i>A little stronger and we'd be evenly matched.</i>

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.030
<i>I'll crush her!</i>

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.740
Ron.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.380
Oh, that call...

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:26.040
You called and it cheapened your hand.
You were in quite a rush.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:29.740
I felt like the player across from 
me had an expensive hand...

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:31.210
How did you know?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:36.030
Wait, can you see through my tiles?!

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.970
You don't need that ability to figure it out.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:42.730
So you did it to end the hand quickly.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:46.830
Hey, hey, but is playing like that fun?
